Use io and string.

Define function atoi taking text as a pointer to TcString returning a whole number:
    Let n be length of text.
    Let i start at 0 as an unsigned number.
    While i < n and text.data[i] equals 32:
        Add 1 to i.
    Let negative be false.
    If i < n and text.data[i] equals 45:
        Set negative to true.
        Add 1 to i.
    Otherwise:
        If i < n and text.data[i] equals 43:
            Add 1 to i.
    Let value start at 0.
    Let digits start at 0.
    While i < n and text.data[i] is at least 48 and text.data[i] is at most 57:
        Let digit be text.data[i] as a whole number - 48.
        Set value to value * 10 + digit.
        Add 1 to i.
        Add 1 to digits.
    If digits is 0:
        Give back 0.
    If negative:
        Set value to 0 - value.
    If value is more than 2147483647:
        Give back 2147483647.
    If value is less than -2147483648:
        Give back -2147483648.
    Give back value.
Done.

Let first be str_from_bytes(bytes_ptr("   -42"), bytes_len("   -42")).
Let second be str_from_bytes(bytes_ptr("4193 with words"), bytes_len("4193 with words")).
Let third be str_from_bytes(bytes_ptr("words and 987"), bytes_len("words and 987")).
Let fourth be str_from_bytes(bytes_ptr("-91283472332"), bytes_len("-91283472332")).
Say atoi(address of first).
Say atoi(address of second).
Say atoi(address of third).
Say atoi(address of fourth).
str_free(address of first).
str_free(address of second).
str_free(address of third).
str_free(address of fourth).
Return 0.
